  "development_type": "Major all other major developments",
  "lapsed_date": "17/04/2011",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The access doorway to the public house shall have a minimum clear width of 900mm, a level surface or ramp between the pavement and the floor and a door handle of not more than 1m above ground level.",
    "Condition : 3 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the extension hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building.",
    "Condition : 4 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 5 - No additional flank windows or other glazed openings shall be formed in the flank wall of the extension hereby approved without the prior written consent of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 6 - The use heeby permitted for a public house shall not take place anywhere on the site except within building[s].",
    "Condition : 7 - The use hereby permitted shall not be open to customers outside the following times 11:00am -11:00pm weekdays and saturdays, 11:00am -10:00pm Sundays and Public Holidays.",
    "Condition : 8 - No amplified or other music shall be played in the premises outside the following times 11:00am - 11:00pm weekdays and Saturday, 11:00am to 10:00pm Sunday and Public Holidays.",
    "Condition : 9 - The use hereby permitted shall be confined to sales to customers attending the premises, and shall not extend to the delivery of food or drink to customers by vehicle.",
    "Condition : 10 - The use hereby permitted for a public house (A4 use) shall not begin until full particulars and details of a scheme to insulate the premises against the transmission of airborne and impact sound between the restaurant and the residential flats above, has been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority. The measures so approved shall be implemented prior to the use commencing and shall be permanently retained thereafter."
  ],
